From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] engine: bare_app: a USB keyboard and mouse

bare_app sends Half-Life the keys of a USB keyboard as Linux key codes
(GAME_MSG_KEY) and the buttons and moves of a USB mouse
(GAME_MSG_MOUSE_*).

Keys become engine keys, so any of them can be bound in the controls
menu; while the engine edits text (the console, chat, text fields) the
characters they type on a US layout go as char events instead, ctrl
with a letter as a control character, as with SDL. The modifiers held
are Platform_GetKeyModifiers'.

In the game the mouse's moves turn the view (Platform_MouseMove) and
its buttons are the mouse's (IN_MouseEvent: attack, attack2); in menus
and the console they move a cursor and click (Platform_GetMousePos),
the wheel is K_MWHEELUP/DOWN. There is no cursor of the system's to
show, so once the mouse has been used an arrow is drawn into each
frame while the engine wants a cursor (host.mouse_visible,
Platform_SetCursorType).

